    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NidJm7Tzd128tJp4sbpQtK)_\n\nHardening found while looking for the Emacs start-up hang. Neither change is shown to cause the hang.\n\n**`sp-tab-inbox`**: both `rg` runs over `~/notes/inbox/tabs/` (the sidebar widget search and the backlink search) were unbounded and synchronous. They now use `sp-tab-inbox-rg-limits` (`--no-config --threads 2 --max-filesize 2M --max-columns 300 --max-columns-preview --max-count 20`), and titles in `sp-tab-inbox-ignored-terms` (\"inbox\", \"home\", \"notes\", ...) are not searched.\n\n**`sp-dashboard`**: the macOS Focus file `~/Library/DoNotDisturb/DB/Assertions.json` is protected (Full Disk Access). Reading it and adding a kqueue watch on its folder, every 30 s while the Dashboard exists, made `tccd` log each refused attempt. The new option `sp-dashboard-read-macos-focus` (default nil) skips both. The flag file `sp-dashboard-focus-flag-file` still works.\n\nOrg docs edited first, `.el` files to match, CHANGELOG entry added. Not run in Emacs (none in the container); parentheses balance checked by script.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBTiUziZidcdSerB8r)_",
